sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Eng as Engineer
    participant AWS as Route53
    participant Tool as migration tooling
    participant Repo as Git repo / PR
    participant GHA as GitHub Actions
    participant CF as Cloudflare
    participant Reg as Registrar
    participant DNS as Public DNS

    Note over Eng,DNS: 1. Preflight
    Eng->>AWS: Lower record TTLs (e.g. 300s) ahead of cutover
    Eng->>Tool: Confirm tooling installed, credentials scoped read-only

    Note over Eng,Repo: 2-4. Export, normalise, validate
    Eng->>AWS: export_route53.sh (list zones + record sets)
    AWS-->>Tool: hosted-zones.json + records-*.json
    Tool->>Tool: convert + JSON Schema validation
    Tool-->>Repo: zones.json + manual-review.json
    Eng->>Repo: Open PR; resolve manual-review items

    Note over GHA: 5. Plan
    Repo->>GHA: CI + terraform-plan
    GHA-->>Repo: Reviewable plan artifact

    Note over Eng,GHA: 6-7. Human review + protected apply
    Eng->>GHA: Review plan, count records
    Eng->>GHA: workflow_dispatch terraform-apply (confirm=apply)
    GHA->>GHA: Protected environment approval
    GHA->>CF: terraform apply (create zones + records)
    CF-->>GHA: zone ids + Cloudflare nameservers

    Note over Eng,DNS: 8. DNS verification (pre-cutover)
    Eng->>CF: Query Cloudflare NS directly; diff vs Route53
    CF-->>Eng: Records match source

    Note over Eng,Reg: 9. Registrar cutover
    Eng->>Reg: Replace Route53 NS with Cloudflare NS
    Reg-->>DNS: Delegation propagates

    Note over Eng,DNS: 10. Rollback decision
    Eng->>DNS: Monitor resolution + application health
    alt Healthy
        Eng->>AWS: Keep Route53 for rollback window, then decommission
    else Problem detected
        Eng->>Reg: Revert NS to Route53 (still authoritative)
    end
